{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The recovery path has a different ordering from normal configuration application: it publishes the snapshot’s `lastApplied`, then calls `RestoreRemotes`, which takes `raftMu`. Recovery blocks the apply worker, while initialized-node stepping and ticks use a separate path.\n\nThat leaves a concrete concurrency question. I’ll register it with the remaining history and scheduling premises explicit; the source ordering alone does not establish unsafe election.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_recovery_candidate.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']))\nsources=[]\ndef s(id,file,a,b):sources.append(dict(id=id,file=file,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind='code_observation'))\ns('src_worker_split','engine.go',1193,1245)\ns('src_recovery_worker','engine.go',274,293)\ns('src_node_tick','node.go',1478,1495)\ns('src_node_step_applied','node.go',1112,1166)\ns('src_snapshot_enqueue','node.go',605,623)\ns('src_rsm_index_ownership','internal/rsm/statemachine.go',160,179)\ns('src_recovery_status_gate','node.go',1389,1448)\ns('src_busy_snapshot','node.go',1258,1298)\nbs={b['id']:b for b in m['behaviors']}\nbs['B_recover']['unknowns']=['During non-initial snapshot recovery, can a step holding raftMu read snapshot-published lastApplied and campaign using pre-snapshot peer membership before RestoreRemotes acquires raftMu?','What legal configuration/snapshot history makes that interval consequential rather than merely an intermediate representation?']\nbs['B_recover']['writes']=['Full restore changes log history and committed/processed index. RSM recover applies snapshot membership and publishes lastApplied under its separate mutex, returns from recover, then calls node.RestoreRemotes, which takes raftMu and updates peer membership.']\nbs['B_recover']['important_branches']=['Initial recovery is protected by node.initialized. For an already initialized node, the apply worker gates on processRecoverStatus, but stepNode checks initialized and handleEvents reads lastApplied before incoming messages.','Recovery busy handling may drop Replicate when the task queue is busy; it does not suppress LocalTick.']\nbs['B_recover']['source_ids']+=['src_worker_split','src_node_step_applied','src_recovery_status_gate','src_busy_snapshot','src_node_tick']\nbs['B_recover']['produces_fact_ids'].append('F_visible_applied')\nbs['B_apply']['produces_fact_ids']=['F_visible_applied']\nbs['B_authority']['consumes_fact_ids'].append('F_visible_applied')\nbs['B_authority']['source_ids'].append('src_node_step_applied')\nbs['B_members']['unknowns']=['Snapshot recovery publishes its applied index before its separate RestoreRemotes callback; whether active stepping can consume it with old peer membership is tracked by B_recover.']\nbs['B_read_confirm']['unknowns']=[]\nbs['B_read_confirm']['external_effects']=['For prefix release, local completions use each saved status context; each remote response uses the corresponding status origin/index but the triggering acknowledgement m.Hint/m.HintHigh. Thus earlier remote contexts differ when the confirming context is later and distinct.']\nbs['B_client']['unknowns']=['Whole-client outcome after receipt of a mismatched remote read context is outside the executed peer-level observation.']\nbs['B_client']['writes'][0]='Batch requests under a nonzero random Low and tick-derived High SystemCtx before Peer.ReadIndex; addReady assigns result index only to an existing exact-context batch.'\nbs['B_client']['source_ids'].append('src_context_generation')\nfor f in m['facts']:\n if f['id']=='F_pending_read':f['unknowns']=[]\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='F_visible_applied',meaning='The state-machine object publishes a last-applied index and term readable by node stepping through GetLastApplied; it reports completed batch application or a locally applied snapshot.',identity={'cluster':'RSM node ClusterID','node':'RSM node NodeID'},validity_context='Current RSM instance. Normal entry batches publish after per-entry node callbacks; snapshot application publishes before the separate RestoreRemotes callback. Publication alone does not assert that every peer-side recovery callback has completed.',representation=['StateMachine.lastApplied.index/term','node.appliedIndex','raft.applied'],durability='In-memory publication, distinct from synchronized on-disk index.',recovery='StateMachine.apply(snapshot) sets published and private applied index/term; RestoreRemotes follows afterward.',source_ids=['src_rsm_index_ownership','src_rsm_applied','src_rsm_dispatch','src_rsm_restore','src_rsm_recover','src_node_step_applied'],unknowns=['Whether campaign admission can consume snapshot publication before peer membership restoration in a consequential legal recovery history.']))\nm['core_overview']['open_details']=['Snapshot recovery publication can precede the raftMu-protected membership callback; investigate actual overlapping step and legal configuration history.','Remote prefix read release preserves the latest context for all remote responses; scoped execution/review is retained in Candidate feedback, not map sources.','Detailed backend crash, transport scheduling and witness persistence variants.']\nm['core_overview']['connection']['explanation']=m['core_overview']['connection']['explanation'].replace('Snapshot recovery has a separately recorded applied-index versus peer-membership interval question.','In contrast to normal entry batches, snapshot application publishes lastApplied before RestoreRemotes obtains raftMu. Whether an initialized-node step can campaign using old membership in that interval remains an explicit question.')\nm['core_overview']['connection']['fact_ids'].append('F_visible_applied')\nm['core_overview']['connection']['source_ids']+=['src_node_step_applied','src_worker_split']\nfor v in m['surfaces']:\n if v['entry_point']=='raft.handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation':v['reason']='The remote branch uses the confirming context for each released request, whereas local release uses each saved context; whole-client effects remain outside the checked peer endpoint.'\n if v['entry_point']=='StateMachine.Recover -> node.RestoreRemotes':v['reason']='Inspect whether active stepping consumes snapshot lastApplied before raftMu-protected peer membership restoration, and construct a legal snapshot membership history if needed.'\njson.dump(m,open('map_recovery.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='Can an initialized node recovering a membership-changing snapshot use the newly published applied index to campaign before the snapshot membership reaches its raft peer?',importance='If old voting membership is used after a newer committed configuration is treated as applied, the election guard intended to prevent nonintersecting decision quorums may be bypassed. This is a potential safety consequence, not a demonstrated election or conflicting decision.',trigger_rationale='Normal entry publication follows configuration callbacks, but StateMachine.apply(snapshot) publishes lastApplied before Recover invokes RestoreRemotes. stepNode holds raftMu and reads GetLastApplied before message processing; RestoreRemotes must acquire that same raftMu. The apply worker recovery gate is not consulted by the step worker. Contract/history and a small controlled publication-overlap exploration should precede any cluster safety claim.',source_ids=['src_rsm_restore','src_rsm_recover','src_node_completion','src_node_step_applied','src_worker_split','src_election_guard','src_recovery_status_gate','src_node_tick'],participants=['Recovering initialized full voter','Snapshot recovery worker','Raft step worker','Existing and snapshot-configuration voters'],objects=['StateMachine.lastApplied','snapshot.Membership','raft.remotes/witnesses','raft.applied','raftMu'],contexts=['Non-initial accepted snapshot whose membership differs from pre-snapshot peer membership','Step/recovery overlap before RestoreRemotes acquires raftMu'],event_paths=['InstallSnapshot -> log.restore -> persistence -> recovery task -> RSM.apply(snapshot) -> GetLastApplied/updateAppliedIndex -> tick/campaign admission -> RestoreRemotes'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B_recover','B_apply','B_authority'],fact_ids=['F_visible_applied'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_members':'Normal configuration callback/publication ordering provides the contrasting producer path and accepted membership update rules.','B_persist':'Snapshot persistence and scheduling establish the recovery input before RSM processing.','B_form':'Potential consequence depends on election quorum and subsequent commitment under the selected membership.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Initial recovery cannot step until initialized; the question excludes it.','Normal applied-entry batches publish only after configuration callbacks return.','Before snapshot applied-index publication, committed>applied blocks campaigning.','Peer term filtering, log freshness, remaining current voters and eventual RestoreRemotes can prevent broader safety consequences even if an old-membership campaign is emitted.'],unknowns=['Can actual recovery publication overlap stepping in the suspected ordering without bypassing another lock or scheduling guard?','Which legal committed configuration/snapshot history produces differing peer membership while preserving local eligibility to campaign?','Does an emitted old-membership campaign suffice for a sourced local responsibility discrepancy, or is a subsequent authority/decision endpoint needed?'],preferred_check='source_review',disposition='needs_specific_evidence')\nchanged={}\nfor id in ['B_recover','B_apply','B_authority']:\n changed[id]=dict(impact='dependency',source_ids=['src_rsm_restore','src_rsm_recover','src_rsm_applied','src_node_step_applied','src_worker_split'],rationale='Record visible applied index producer/consumer dependency and distinguish recovery publication from peer membership callback completion.',preserves='C_remote_read_context still concerns stable-term remote read confirmation and exact context consumption. It does not depend on snapshot recovery, and its authority filtering and observed scope are unchanged.')\nfor id in ['B_members','B_read_confirm','B_client','F_pending_read','core_overview']:\n changed[id]=dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['src_rsm_restore','src_confirmation_emission','src_read_complete','src_context_generation','src_node_step_applied'],rationale='Replace answered or overgeneral open questions with conditional source relationships; keep separate recovery and client-endpoint limits.',preserves='No identity, normative read-correlation requirement, counterevidence, execution input or observation scope changes. F_pending_read meaning remains the stored original request context; only its answered remote-correlation unknown is removed.')\nx=dict(action='continue',question=q,map_path='map_recovery.json',map_changes=changed,sources=sources,rationale='Reselect the independent recovery publication/context validity question after the remote read-context finding is confirmed.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['B_recover','B_authority','F_pending_read','e76c3db2b24c4948854ba37f79813406','606dd79be1bc46bb8c55ab57347d7089','bcdb369fb89e4195bfbf79fde7e484f3','src_worker_split','src_node_step_applied'],answered='The controller assessment now confirms C_remote_read_context violated with completed correspondence review. Related map entries retain the actual conditional remote-response behavior and remove the answered context question; wider client effects remain excluded. Recovery source investigation shows a distinct publication path: snapshot apply sets visible lastApplied before RestoreRemotes takes raftMu. Initialized-node stepping independently takes raftMu, reads visible lastApplied and processes ticks; recovery status gating is in apply processing, while busy recovery only conditionally discards Replicate messages. This sources an overlap question but does not execute it or establish an unsafe election.',remaining=q['unknowns'],understanding='updated',rationale='The next discriminator is a concrete cross-worker publication ordering and its legal membership history, not another variant of the confirmed read-context mismatch.'))\njson.dump(x,open('submission6.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_recovery_candidate.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));z=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission6.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(z.stdout);print(z.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
